  "description": "Madonna V3.2 Öhlins Rolling Chassis\n\nThe Madonna is the most capable, adjustable and durable bike we’ve ever built. With either 29-inch wheels or a mullet setup, 160 mm of rear travel and a 170 mm fork, the Madonna is ready for any trail, bike park or race track.\nWith the Rolling Chassis Kit we offer you a high-quality foundation for your individual Madonna build. You'll be ready to go in no time with the included component package yet still have plenty of room to create your own personal bike masterpiece – who wants an off the shelf build anyway?\nWe provide a Öhlins RXF38 m.3 fork with the frame, which you can combine with your preferred Öhlins or Fox shock at the rear. We also offer the Rolling Chassis with Fox forks – click here for that.\nIncluded is a OneUp Components V3 Dropper, with the choice of drop starting at 150 mm and going all the way up to 240 mm of travel, to provide the optimal setup for every rider. Their V3 handlebar remote is also included. If you need some help determining the amount of drop for you, click here.\nFor the cockpit, we rely again on OneUp Components and offer you the stem in two lengths of 42 mm or 50 mm and their carbon handlebar with either 20 mm or 35 mm rise, so you can feel comfortable from the get go. Ergon’s GDH Team grips and SM10 Enduro saddle round out the touch points. If you're unsure which combination of stem and bar is best for you, click here for more information on the perfect cockpit setup.\nThe Rolling Chassis can be topped off with the with the optional DT Swiss EX1700 or Newmen Beskar 30 Enduro wheels. Both are available as full 29\" or 29\"/27.5\" options and you can choose between Sram XD or Shimano Microspline freehubs. You receive the Maxxis Assegai with EXO+ casing up front and a Maxxis Minion DHR II with DD casing for 29\" and EXO+ casing for 27,5\" out back on top. This combination is our current go-to in almost all conditions. The Maxxis tyres, rim tape and valves are a bonus to the wheels, if you decide to order your rolling chassis without wheels, those components will not be included.\nTo get you off to a good start in building your new bike, we've already pressed the headset cups into the frame and mounted the crown race on the fork. The tubeless tape and valves are also installed, you’ll just need to add in some sealant. The rest of the components are ready for you to assemble – this way you can truly experience the build process from the ground up and get to know your new bike and all its technical details. But you’re never on your own, as our support is always there if you need help building and can’t find the answer you’re after in our extensive knowledge base.\nTo learn more about the Madonna, you can find all details here.",
